{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778976725543,"sessionID":"ses_1ccba0f2dffeVPd0wy4yf6tXOs","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_JtIiHISXMDuzAxvtGrXzgFpo","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl.Makefile","offset":1,"limit":220},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl.Makefile</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ## Customize Makefile settings for cl\n2: ##\n3: ## If you need to customize your Makefile, make\n4: ## changes here rather than in the main Makefile\n5: # railing-whitespace  xref-syntax\n6: \n7: \n8: # ----------------------------------------\n9: # BUILDING RELEASE PRODUCTS\n10: # ----------------------------------------\n11: \n12: # Preprocessing: automatically generate text definitions from logical definitions\n13: $(EDIT_PREPROCESSED): $(SRC) | all_robot_plugins\n14: \t$(ROBOT) flybase:rewrite-def -i $< --dot-definitions --null-definitions \\\n15: \t\t                     --no-ids --filter-prefix CL_ \\\n16: \t\t                     --add-annotation \"oboInOwl:hasDbXref FBC:Autogenerated\" \\\n17: \t\t                     -o $@\n18: \n19: # Building CL-plus (CL + PCL product)\n20: # HACK: We have to remove the disjointness axioms between taxa, because\n21: # PCL does not enforce taxon constraints and may contain TC violations\n22: # that would be revealed here due to the presence of those axioms\n23: # (thereby causing that step to fail). The proper fix would be for PCL\n24: # to enforce TC.\n25: # See <https://github.com/obophenotype/provisional_cell_ontology/issues/59>\n26: cl-plus.owl: $(ONT)-full.owl\n27: \t$(ROBOT) merge -i $< -I $(OBOBASE)/pcl/pcl-base.owl \\\n28: \t\t unmerge -I $(OBOBASE)/ncbitaxon/subsets/taxslim-disjoint-over-in-taxon.owl \\\n29: \t\t reason --reasoner WHELK --equivalent-classes-allowed asserted-only \\\n30: \t\t        --exclude-tautologies structural \\\n31: \t\t relax \\\n32: \t\t reduce --reasoner WHELK \\\n33: \t\t $(SHARED_ROBOT_COMMANDS) \\\n34: \t\t annotate --ontology-iri $(ONTBASE)/$@ \\\n35: \t\t $(ANNOTATE_ONTOLOGY_VERSION) --output $@\n36: \n37: # Main release artefact (cl.owl)\n38: # We override the standard ODK-generate rule so that we can merge in the\n39: # tags for the taxon subsets.\n40: POSTPROCESS_ADDITIONS = subsets/human-tags.ofn \\\n41:                         subsets/mouse-tags.ofn\n42: $(ONT).owl: $(ONT)-full.owl $(POSTPROCESS_ADDITIONS)\n43: \t$(ROBOT) merge -i $< $(foreach add,$(POSTPROCESS_ADDITIONS),-i $(add)) \\\n44: \t\t annotate --ontology-iri $(URIBASE)/$@ $(ANNOTATE_ONTOLOGY_VERSION) \\\n45: \t\t convert -o $@\n46: \n47: \n48: # ----------------------------------------\n49: # SSSOM MAPPINGS\n50: # ----------------------------------------\n51: \n52: # CL's \"local\" mapping set (extracted from cross-references).\n53: # The long list of \"prefix-to-predicate\" mapping is necessary because CL\n54: # does not contain the oboInOwl:treat-xrefs-as-... annotations that are\n55: # supposed to provide those mappings.\n56: $(MAPPINGDIR)/cl-local.sssom.tsv: $(SRC) | all_robot_plugins\n57: \t$(ROBOT) sssom:xref-extract -i $< --mapping-file $@ -v --drop-duplicates \\\n58: \t\t                    --prefix 'FMA:   http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma' \\\n59: \t\t                    --prefix 'KUPO:  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/KUPO_'  \\\n60: \t\t                    --prefix 'SCTID: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SCTID_' \\\n61: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'AEO http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch' \\\n62: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'CARO http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch' \\\n63: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'GO http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch' \\\n64: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'VSAO http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch' \\\n65: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'VHOG http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broadMatch' \\\n66: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'EV http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrowMatch' \\\n67: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'NCIT http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrowMatch' \\\n68: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'SCTID http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrowMatch' \\\n69: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'AAO https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n70: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'EHDAA2 https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n71: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'EMAPA https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n72: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'FMA https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n73: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'KUPO https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n74: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'MA https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n75: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'WBbt https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n76: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'XAO https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n77: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'ZFA https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n78: \t\t                    --set-id http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/cl.sssom.tsv \\\n79: \t> $(REPORTDIR)/cl-xrefs-extraction.txt\n80: \n81: # CL's \"meta\" mapping set, made by compiling the \"local\" set above\n82: # with the sets obtained from FBbt and ZFA below.\n83: $(MAPPINGDIR)/cl.sssom.tsv: $(MAPPINGDIR)/cl-local.sssom.tsv \\\n84: \t\t\t    $(MAPPINGDIR)/fbbt.sssom.tsv \\\n85: \t\t\t    $(MAPPINGDIR)/zfa.sssom.tsv\n86: \tsssom-cli $(foreach src, $^, -i $(src)) \\\n87: \t\t  --prefix-map-from-input \\\n88: \t\t  --rule 'object==CL:* -> invert()' \\\n89: \t\t  --rule 'subject==CL:* -> include()' \\\n90: \t\t  --output $@\n91: \n92: # Remote mapping sets\n93: # -------------------\n94: \n95: EXTERNAL_SSSOM_PROVIDERS = fbbt zfa\n96: EXTERNAL_SSSOM_SETS = $(foreach provider, $(EXTERNAL_SSSOM_PROVIDERS), $(MAPPINGDIR)/$(provider).sssom.tsv)\n97: \n98: # We only refresh external resources under MIR=true\n99: ifeq ($(strip $(MIR)),true)\n100: \n101: # FBbt mapping set\n102: $(MAPPINGDIR)/fbbt.sssom.tsv: .FORCE\n103: \twget -O - \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fbbt/fbbt.sssom.tsv\" | \\\n104: \t\tsssom-cli --prefix-map-from-input \\\n105: \t\t          --include 'object==CL:*' \\\n106: \t\t          --update-from-ontology $(SRC):object,label,existence \\\n107: \t\t          --output $@\n108: \n109: # ZFA mapping set (extracted from ZFA cross-references).\n110: # ZFA does contain oboInOwl:treat-xrefs-as-... annotations, but here\n111: # it's easier to ignore them, as this automatically filters out all the\n112: # xrefs that point to anything else than CL.\n113: # 1. Create intermediate set from ZFA.\n114: $(TMPDIR)/zfa.sssom.tsv: .FORCE | all_robot_plugins\n115: \t$(ROBOT) sssom:xref-extract -I http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/zfa.owl \\\n116: \t\t                    --mapping-file $@ -v --drop-duplicates \\\n117: \t\t                    --ignore-treat-xrefs \\\n118: \t\t                    --map-prefix-to-predicate 'CL https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/crossSpeciesExactMatch' \\\n119: \t\t                    --set-id http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/zfa/zfa.sssom.tsv \\\n120: \t> $(REPORTDIR)/xfa-xrefs-extraction\n121: \n122: # 2. Create definitive ZFA set by checking against CL's contents\n123: $(MAPPINGDIR)/zfa.sssom.tsv: $(TMPDIR)/zfa.sssom.tsv $(SRC)\n124: \tsssom-cli -i $< --update-from-ontology $(SRC):object,label,existence,source -o $@\n125: \n126: endif\n127: \n128: # Mappings component\n129: # ------------------\n130: # The mappings.owl component is derived from the remote mapping sets\n131: # (as fetched above). It contains old-style cross-references to make\n132: # those mappings \"visible\" to CL editors and users in the usual way.\n133: $(COMPONENTSDIR)/mappings.owl: $(SRC) $(EXTERNAL_SSSOM_SETS) | all_robot_plugins\n134: \t$(ROBOT) sssom:inject -i $< \\\n135: \t\t\t      $(foreach set, $(EXTERNAL_SSSOM_SETS), --sssom $(set)) \\\n136: \t\t\t      --ruleset $(SCRIPTSDIR)/mappings-to-xrefs.rules \\\n137: \t\t\t      --error-on-unshortenable-iris \\\n138: \t\t\t      --no-merge --bridge-file $@ \\\n139: \t\t\t      --bridge-iri http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/components/mappings.owl\n140: \n141: \n142: # ----------------------------------------\n143: # TAXON CONSTRAINTS CHECK\n144: # ----------------------------------------\n145: \n146: # The TC check requires te taxslim-disjoint-over-in-taxon.owl ontology,\n147: # which is declared as an ODK mirror (under the name ncbitaxondisjoints)\n148: # and as such should already have been downloaded into the mirror\n149: # directory by the standard ODK-generated rule. But the QC checks are\n150: # typically run under MIR=false, so while the standard rule would be\n151: # invoked by Make it would not result in the mirror being downloaded.\n152: # So instead, we make the TC check depend on another file, and here we\n153: # 1. force the download of the mirror if it is not already there;\n154: # 2. create a link to that mirror.\n155: $(TMPDIR)/taxslim-disjoint-over-in-taxon.owl:\n156: \tif [ ! -f $(MIRRORDIR)/ncbitaxondisjoints.owl ]; then \\\n157: \t\t$(MAKE) $(MIRRORDIR)/ncbitaxondisjoints.owl MIR=true IMP=true ; \\\n158: \tfi && \\\n159: \tln -f -s ../$(MIRRORDIR)/ncbitaxondisjoints.owl $@\n160: \n161: # Actual TC check: we add the taxon disjointness axioms into the\n162: # ontology, make sure to expand all macros, then try to reason over the\n163: # resulting product.\n164: $(REPORTDIR)/taxon-constraint-check.txt: $(EDIT_PREPROCESSED) $(TMPDIR)/taxslim-disjoint-over-in-taxon.owl\n165: \t$(ROBOT) merge $(foreach src,$^,-i $(src)) \\\n166: \t\t expand -o $(TMPDIR)/cl-plus-taxon-disjoints.ofn \\\n167: \t\t reason -r WHELK > $@\n168: \n169: # Include the TC check in the routine tests\n170: test: $(REPORTDIR)/taxon-constraint-check.txt\n171: \n172: \n173: # ----------------------------------------\n174: # OTHER CUSTOM CHECKS\n175: # ----------------------------------------\n176: \n177: .PHONY: obocheck\n178: obocheck: $(SRC) | all_robot_plugins\n179: \t$(ROBOT) merge -i $(SRC) \\\n180: \t\t remove --base-iri $(URIBASE)/CL_ --axioms external --trim false \\\n181: \t\t convert --check false -f obo $(OBO_FORMAT_OPTIONS) \\\n182: \t\t         --output $(TMPDIR)/cl-check.obo\n183: \tfastobo-validator $(TMPDIR)/cl-check.obo\n184: \n185: test_obsolete: $(ONT).obo\n186: \t! grep \"! obsolete\" $<\n187: \n188: test: obocheck \\\n189:       test_obsolete\n190: \n191: \n192: # ----------------------------------------\n193: # TAXON SUBSETS\n194: # ----------------------------------------\n195: \n196: TAXON_ID_human = NCBITaxon:9606\n197: TAXON_ID_mouse = NCBITaxon:10090\n198: \n199: # Create a taxon-specific subset. This rule creates two distinct files:\n200: # (1) the subset proper (subsets/%-view.owl), which can be used on its\n201: #     own (and can be published as a release artifact if desired);\n202: # (2) a small containing oboInOwl:inSubset annotations to \"tag\" all\n203: #     terms that belong to the subset (subsets/%-tags.ofn); that file\n204: #     can then be combined with a CL release product.\n205: .PRECIOUS: subsets/%-view.owl\n206: subsets/%-view.owl subsets/%-tags.ofn: $(ONT)-full.owl | all_robot_plugins\n207: \t$(ROBOT) expand --input $< --expand-term RO:0002161 \\\n208: \t\t uberon:create-species-subset --taxon $(TAXON_ID_$*) \\\n209: \t\t                              --strategy precise \\\n210: \t\t                              --reasoner WHELK \\\n211: \t\t                              --root CL:0000000 \\\n212: \t\t                              --prefix 'cl: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl#' \\\n213: \t\t                              --subset-name cl:$*_subset \\\n214: \t\t                              --only-tag-in CL: \\\n215: \t\t                              --write-tags-to subsets/$*-tags.ofn \\\n216: \t\t reason --reasoner WHELK --equivalent-classes-allowed all \\\n217: \t\t        --exclude-tautologies structural \\\n218: \t\t relax \\\n219: \t\t remove --axioms equivalent \\\n220: \t\t reduce --reasoner WHELK \\\n\n(Showing lines 1-220 of 401. Use offset=221 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Customize Makefile settings for cl\n##\n## If you need to customize your Makefile, make\n## changes here rather than in the main Makefile\n# railing-whitespace  xref-syntax\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------\n# BUILDING RELEASE PRODUCTS\n# ----------------------------------------\n\n# Preprocessing: automatically generate text definitions from logical definitions\n$(EDIT_PREPROCESSED): $(SRC) | all_robot_plugins\n\t$(ROBOT) flybase:rewrite-def -i $< --dot-definitions --null-definitions \\\n\t\t                     --no-ids --filter-prefix CL_ \\\n\t\t                     --add-annotation \"oboInOwl:hasDbXref FBC:Autogenerated\" \\\n\t\t                     -o $@\n\n# Building CL-plus (CL + PCL product)\n# HACK: We have to remove the disjointness axioms between taxa, because","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/cl.Makefile","time":{"start":1778976725532,"end":1778976725541}},"id":"prt_e3346975a0013Swzyk29RzUm7l","sessionID":"ses_1ccba0f2dffeVPd0wy4yf6tXOs","messageID":"msg_e33468e74001C7I1NI5jwgU05h"}}
